<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">26072026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Saudi aircraft struck Hodeida, the port through which most of Yemen's food and fuel arrive, wounding two people... and Yemeni forces answered with missiles against an air base, a refinery and the oil terminal at Yanbu.</s> <s>Hodeida has been bombed before, and each time the throughput of wheat and diesel into a country living with famine conditions has fallen with it.</s> <s>Yemen's forces now threaten to close the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, which carries about twelve percent of world trade, and no mediator has yet said who would reopen it.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Iran says a Ukrainian drone struck one of its commercial vessels in the Caspian Sea, killing a sailor and wounding another.</s> <s>The Caspian is a closed sea ringed by Iran, Russia, Kazakhstan, Turkmenistan and Azerbaijan, and it's the corridor through which Iranian and Russian trade moves around Western sanctions — which means a war fought on the Black Sea has now reached water no combatant shares a shore with.</s> <s>Tehran has invoked Article Two, paragraph four of the UN Charter and asked the Security Council to act, while Kyiv says only that the ships carried military cargo, a claim nobody outside the two governments has verified.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>An Israeli strike in Gaza killed the territory's police chief, Al-Maqadma, along with four others.</s> <s>Israel's military describes Gaza's police as members of Hamas's armed wing; the same officers are the force residents depend on to move aid convoys and keep order at distribution points, so the distinction decides whether food reaches people.</s> <s>Mediators in Cairo, Doha, Ankara and Washington have announced nothing since, and the policing of hunger in Gaza is now a question with no institution behind it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>At least thirty-five people burned to death when a bus caught fire on the highway between Damascus and Deir Ezzor.</s> <s>That road crosses desert wrecked by more than a decade of war, with no hospital anywhere along it — the defence ministry had to evacuate survivors by helicopter, which is what a country does when its ambulances have nowhere to drive to.</s> <s>Syria's Civil Defence says it answered nineteen other road accidents the day before, so the fire wasn't an aberration... it was the worst hour of an ordinary week.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Sudan's army chief, Abdel Fattah al-Burhan, toured Asmara and secured an invitation to Uganda before so much as touching Washington's draft ceasefire text.</s> <s>He's assembling regional cover first, which is how every Sudanese belligerent since independence has approached negotiation — the patron is settled before the position is.</s> <s>Meanwhile Rapid Support Forces drones killed along the border with Chad, and Burhan wants a withdrawal from the cities before he'll discuss anything else.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>At least a dozen herders have disappeared in Mauritania's Guidimakha region since January while crossing into Mali.</s> <s>Local officials blame Malian forces and Russia's Africa Corps, and they point to something bleaker still: the same herders move safely across ground held by al-Qaeda affiliates, because there they pay a pasture fee and are left alone.</s> <s>More than three hundred thousand Malian refugees are already sheltering in Mauritania, in a country whose own herders now find the state more dangerous than the insurgency.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Brazil refused entry to two senior American diplomats who'd planned to inspect its electoral system before the October fourth vote.</s> <s>Brasília's foreign ministry confirmed the denial, and there's no treaty obliging Brazil to admit foreign officials to examine its ballots — an electronic system with a decades-long public audit record behind it.</s> <s>What's being tested here isn't the machinery of the vote but whether a large Southern democracy can decline supervision without consequence.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Kuwait sold forty-nine percent of its oil pipelines to Blackstone, <sub alias="K K R">KKR</sub> and Brookfield for sixteen billion dollars.</s> <s>The buyers take a long-term lease over three hundred and twenty kilometres of pipe, and Kuwait's raising the money to repair damage from nearly fourteen hundred Iranian missile and drone strikes — war costs converted directly into foreign claims on national infrastructure.</s> <s>The lease fixes tariffs and dividend priorities for decades, meaning Kuwaitis not yet born will pay a schedule set during a war they didn't choose.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Standing beside Vladimir Putin in Omsk, Kazakhstan's president Kassym-Jomart Tokayev called for a truce in Ukraine.</s> <s>Kazakhstan is landlocked and ships most of its oil through Russian pipelines, a dependency that normally keeps Astana silent — the country learned in twenty twenty-two how quickly that pipeline develops technical faults when Moscow is displeased.</s> <s>Russian state media covered the meeting and left the ceasefire remark out of it entirely.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan froze fuel prices this weekend, and the reason is almost comic: Platts, a pricing service in London, doesn't publish benchmarks on Saturdays.</s> <s>Under its <sub alias="I M F">IMF</sub> programme Islamabad passes global fuel prices through to consumers on a fixed schedule, so a British firm's calendar sets what a rickshaw driver in Multan pays.</s> <s>Diesel, which moves freight and therefore food, rose faster than petrol at four rupees eighty a litre — the cost will surface in vegetable prices before the next review.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Nearly two hundred thousand people have been displaced by wildfires in France and Spain, with the suburbs of Bordeaux emptied and forty-four thousand evacuated from the Cap Ferret peninsula.</s> <s>Suppression capacity is the binding number here: fire services are sized against a historical fire season, and when the season lengthens and the fires burn hotter, the shortfall shows up as evacuation rather than extinguishing.</s> <s>Winds are forecast to push the blaze near Madrid further, and Emmanuel Macron has asked the European Union for reinforcement.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Scotland's Cairngorms, five hundred firefighters have fought a single fire for ten days.</s> <s>It's burning in peat, and that's a different animal from a forest fire — the carbon stored underground smoulders below the surface where rain can't reach it, so the blaze survives the weather that would end a grass fire.</s> <s>Police evacuated Nethy Bridge overnight when the wind turned, and First Minister John Swinney has asked London for military assistance.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India is confronting a quiet failure in its fertility clinics: embryo mix-ups that give a child the wrong parents.</s> <s>Every embryo passes through retrieval, fertilisation, freezing and transfer, and any one of those steps can mislabel it — which is why India's new assisted reproduction law mandates clinic registration and audits rather than trusting the laboratory bench.</s> <s>A national registry now tracks clinics, but inspectors remain few, and a registry without inspection is a list, not a safeguard.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>SpaceX's Starship came through reentry with its eighteen thousand ceramic tiles intact.</s> <s>The next attempt is catching the ship on the launch tower itself, which demands near-zero arrival error against a fixed structure the vehicle destroys if it misses — reusability, not thrust, is what makes the economics work.</s> <s>Orbital refuelling, which NASA's Moon landings depend on entirely, still hasn't been demonstrated even once.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>North Korea has arrested its own state hackers.</s> <s>The units blamed for the majority of the world's cryptocurrency theft allegedly diverted funds from Pyongyang's own central bank into overseas wallets, which is the structural hazard of building a treasury out of untraceable money — the state can't audit what it designed to be unauditable.</s> <s>The account comes from Daily <sub alias="N K">NK</sub>, a defector-linked outlet, and couldn't be independently confirmed.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Humans once spoke as many as seventy-five thousand languages.</s> <s>A computational model built from hunter-gatherer population proxies puts that peak somewhere between three thousand and one thousand years ago, with the decline beginning as multinational empires standardised the language of administration — and colonialism accelerating the collapse rather than starting it.</s> <s>Roughly seven thousand remain, and the researchers, led by Damián Blasi, are describing the shape of a loss that's still in progress.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>